    "contentEn": "## Origins in the Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn\n\nIn late 19th-century London, the esoteric society known as the **Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn** gathered scholars of Kabbalah, Hermeticism, and astrology. Occultist **Arthur Edward Waite** spearheaded an ambitious endeavor: to synthesize sacred mystery traditions into a universal 78-card visual lexicon.\n\n---\n\n## Pamela Colman Smith: The Intuitive Genius Behind the Art\n\nWaite partnered with visionary artist **Pamela Colman Smith (Pixie)**. In a fever of inspiration spanning roughly six months, Smith hand-illustrated all 78 cards in pen and watercolor. Her iconic pictorial scenes transformed the Minor Arcana into living psychological narratives, establishing the timeless gold standard for tarot across the globe."
